    "body": "@bzbarsky It turns out that only Firefox postpones creation of style sheets during DOM insertions. In Chrome, Safari and Edge, scripts that are inserted at the same time as style elements can observe the stylesheets during their execution.\r\n\r\nSee [this assertion](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/15264/commits/5082ab66dbe7c24b3a62f86251fc1ba81de79690#diff-e454c28d2f53c313161aa05dbdeca653R19) and [this comment](https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/576#issuecomment-462708226).\r\n\r\nNote also that delaying the creation of the stylesheet until all prior scripts have been executed also cause weird issues if those prior scripts change the stylesheet on their own, causing the stylesheet to be [recreated twice](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/15264/commits/5082ab66dbe7c24b3a62f86251fc1ba81de79690#diff-e454c28d2f53c313161aa05dbdeca653R36), because they don't have a concept of having already been recreated, unlike scripts and their \"already started\" flag.",
    "created_at": "2019-02-12T10:44:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-12-09T13:13:57Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/4354#discussion_r255897129",
